-0834805f4b83" :question/id #uuid "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83"] [:db/add "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -12 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 19 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?"] [:db/add "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{33}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -12 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}+5R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -12 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 19 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}+5R_{3}$."] [:db/add "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83" :question/answer-fields "e82a5548-61f0-57e7-8656-f413cdeb6b8a"] [:db/ensure "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186161967 :knowledge-point/questions "67c128fe-70eb-5467-8398-0834805f4b83"] [:db/add "ca38758b-f063-5ec5-a803-20e0efdb567b" :answer/id #uuid "ca38758b-f063-5ec5-a803-20e0efdb567b"] [:db/add "ca38758b-f063-5ec5-a803-20e0efdb567b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "ca38758b-f063-5ec5-a803-20e0efdb567b" :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1}-9R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-R_{3}$"] [:db/ensure "ca38758b-f063-5ec5-a803-20e0efdb567b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d5d33d2a-74a5-52c8-8090-92d9178a31a3" :answer/id #uuid "d5d33d2a-74a5-52c8-8090-92d9178a31a3"] [:db/add "d5d33d2a-74a5-52c8-8090-92d9178